#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:1
msgid "Bounds Checks: Pay Once or Opt Out"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:3
msgid ""
"Every `a[i]` in a kernel hides a safety check. The compiler turns it into "
"\"is `i` inside the slice? If not, stop the kernel\" -- a compare and a "
"branch, on every access, in every thread. On a CPU you rarely notice. In a "
"GPU hot loop you do: the naive GEMM in the `gemm` example spends most of its "
"inner loop on two such checks per multiply-add and reaches about 2,940 "
"GFLOPS on an RTX 5090. The same kernel with the checks removed runs at 7,160 "
"GFLOPS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:11
msgid ""
"This chapter is about closing that gap without giving up safety. It builds "
"on [the safety model](the-safety-model.md): you already know that "
"`DisjointSlice` makes parallel writes race-free and that a checked "
"`PreparedLaunch` proves launch geometry on the host. The same idea -- check "
"a fact once, in the right place, and carry the proof in a type -- extends to "
"reads and to buffer sizes."
msgstr ""

