#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:133
msgid "Views and barriers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:135
msgid ""
"One rule when a kernel uses `sync_threads()`: every thread must reach the "
"barrier, so a thread whose view check failed must not return early. Fall "
"back to an empty view instead, and let reads degrade to a fill value:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:139
msgid ""
"let a_row = a_mat.row(row, k).unwrap_or(RowView32::empty());\n"
"// ... later, in the staging loop:\n"
"tile[idx] = a_row.get(i).unwrap_or(0.0);   // one compare, zero-fill at "
"edges\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:145
msgid ""
"`get` costs a single compare -- this is the accessor for edges, not for hot "
"loops. The tiled kernel in `gemm_views` uses exactly this pattern."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:150
msgid "Writing the result: a tile with a runtime row width"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:152
msgid ""
"The safe way to *write* is still `DisjointSlice`, as described in [the "
"safety model](the-safety-model.md). What's new is `tile_2d32_rt`: the 2D "
"tile whose row width is a runtime value like `n`, for output matrices whose "
"size isn't known at compile time:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:157
msgid ""
"// `c` carries its own row width, bound on the host to this same `n`,\n"
"// so the call is safe: no per-thread width crosses the call.\n"
"if let Some(mut cell) = c.tile_2d32_rt(coord) {\n"
"    let previous = cell.at_const::<0, 0>().read();\n"
"    cell.at_const::<0, 0>().write(alpha * sum + beta * previous);\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:166
msgid ""
"Why does the width come from the slice and not from an argument? The tile-"
"disjointness argument -- \"distinct thread coordinates own non-overlapping "
"rectangles\" -- silently assumes all threads agree on the row width. Two "
"threads that disagree describe two different grids over the same memory: "
"with 1x1 tiles, thread `(1, 0)` with width 5 resolves flat index `1*5 + 0 = "
"5`, and thread `(0, 5)` with width 100 resolves `0*100 + 5 = 5`. Same "
"element, two `&mut`, a data race."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:174
msgid ""
"An earlier design took the width as an `unsafe` per-call argument, but no "
"call-site obligation can close that hole: safe code can select between two "
"\"uniform\" widths under a thread-varying condition. So the row width lives "
"in the slice instead. The host binds it once for the launch through "
"`cuda_host::RowWidth`, device code cannot choose it, and every thread that "
"addresses `c` reads the same width by construction. When the width *is* "
"known at compile time, use `tile_2d32` instead and a mismatch becomes a type "
"error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:185
msgid "`requires`: promise the sizes at launch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:187
msgid ""
"The views check strips against `a.len()` at runtime because nothing else "
"guarantees the buffers are big enough. But the host *knows* the sizes -- it "
"allocated the buffers. The `requires` key on a launch contract writes that "
"knowledge down, next to the kernel:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:192
msgid ""
"#[kernel(launch_context = lc)]\n"
"#[launch_bounds(256)]\n"
"#[launch_contract(domain = 2, coordinates = u32, block = (16, 16, 1),\n"
"    requires = (k >= 1, a.len() >= m * k, b.len() >= k * n, c.len() >= m * "
"n))]\n"
"pub fn sgemm_naive_views(m: u32, n: u32, k: u32, alpha: f32,\n"
"    a: &[f32], b: &[f32], beta: f32,\n"
"    mut c: DisjointSlice<f32, RuntimeRowMajorTiles<1, 1>>) {\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:202
msgid ""
"The generated launcher evaluates every relation once per launch, on the CPU, "
"before anything touches the GPU. A launch that breaks a relation doesn't "
"fault mid-kernel -- it returns an error that names the promise:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:206
msgid ""
"sgemm_naive_views: size requirement `a.len() >= m * k` violated:\n"
"left-hand side is 8192, right-hand side is 16384\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:211
msgid ""
"Relations are deliberately *not* arbitrary Rust. Each one is a single "
"comparison built from slice parameters as `name.len()`, unsigned integer "
"scalar parameters, integer literals, parentheses, and `+ - *`. Two reasons:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:215
msgid ""
"Every identifier is validated against the kernel's actual parameter list, so "
"a typo is a compile error, not a check against the wrong value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:218
msgid ""
"Every `+`, `-`, `*` compiles to checked `u64` arithmetic, so a huge `m * k` "
"cannot wrap around to a small number and falsely pass."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:221
msgid ""
"The `_unchecked` launcher variants skip these checks, exactly as they skip "
"the geometry checks; upholding the relations becomes part of their `SAFETY` "
"contract."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:227
msgid "The escape hatch: `unchecked_indexing`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:229
msgid ""
"Sometimes no view fits the access pattern, and you've verified the kernel is "
"correct. For that case there is a blunt instrument:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:232
msgid ""
"#[kernel(unchecked_indexing)]\n"
"pub fn hot_loop(a: &[f32], b: &[f32], mut c: DisjointSlice<f32>) {\n"
"    let idx = thread::index_1d().get();\n"
"    if let Some(out) = c.get_mut(thread::index_1d()) {\n"
"        *out = a[idx] + b[idx];   // no check, no trap\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:242
msgid ""
"The flag deletes the check behind every `a[i]` in the kernel. The contract "
"is `get_unchecked`'s: you promise every index is in bounds, and if you're "
"wrong the result is undefined behavior -- no trap, possibly silent "
"corruption of unrelated memory. It doesn't require the `unsafe` keyword, but "
"treat it as if it did."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:248
msgid "There is also a whole-build switch for experiments:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:250
msgid ""
"$ CUDA_OXIDE_UNCHECKED_INDEXING=1 cargo oxide build my_example\n"
"$ cargo oxide build my_example --unchecked-indexing   # same thing\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:255
msgid "Scope, precisely:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:257
msgid ""
"Only indexing checks (`a[i]`) are removed. Arithmetic overflow, division by "
"zero, and every other safety check still traps. Range indexing (`&a[i..j]`) "
"also still traps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:260
msgid ""
"The per-kernel flag covers that kernel's body, including functions inlined "
"into it. It never leaks: a kernel that calls a flagged kernel's helper "
"function keeps its own checks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:263
msgid ""
"Turn it on only after the checked build passes, ideally under `compute-"
"sanitizer`. The [`unchecked_indexing`](https://github.com/NVlabs/cuda-oxide/"
"tree/main/crates/rustc-codegen-cuda/examples/unchecked_indexing) example "
"shows the PTX with and without the flag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:270
msgid "Choosing between them"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:272
msgid ""
"Can a view express the access pattern (rows, columns, tiles, dot products)?\n"
"├── yes -> use views + a `requires` contract.  Safe, and measurably as\n"
"│          fast as raw pointers.\n"
"└── no  -> is the kernel verified correct (sanitizer, tests)?\n"
"    ├── yes -> #[kernel(unchecked_indexing)], documented like unsafe code.\n"
"    └── no  -> keep the checks. 2,900 GFLOPS with traps beats\n"
"               garbage at 7,000.\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:282
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:284
msgid ""
"`a[i]` costs a compare and a branch per access, and in hot loops that is the "
"dominant cost -- 2.4x on naive GEMM."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:286
msgid ""
"Read views (`MatrixView32::row` / `col`, `zip_exact`) check a whole strip "
"once and make every read inside it check-free. Fully safe, and the PTX "
"matches hand-written unsafe code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:289
msgid ""
"`requires = (...)` moves buffer-size checks to the host: one typed error per "
"launch instead of a mid-kernel trap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/bounds-checks.md:291
msgid ""
"`#[kernel(unchecked_indexing)]` deletes indexing checks outright. Same "
"contract as `get_unchecked`; out of bounds is undefined behavior."
msgstr ""
